# Cooldown on newly published releases — see SECURITY.md "Dependency
# vulnerabilities". `pnpm audit` matches against an advisory database, so it is
# blind to a compromised-maintainer release by construction: a freshly
# malicious version has no advisory yet. Age is the defence that works there —
# such releases are typically yanked within hours.
#
# 10080 minutes = 7 days, matching `minimumReleaseAge` in .github/renovate.json.
# This one covers the manual path SECURITY.md points at (`pnpm update`,
# `pnpm add`), which Renovate never sees. It does not affect
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, so CI is unchanged.
#
# Requires pnpm >= 10.16; older versions ignore the key.
minimum-release-age=10080
